  "difficulty_level": "H3",
  "difficulty_reason": "The counted theorem identifies the leading monomial of every homogeneous component above the minimal degree for all ascending term orders, and its proof is not a computation: it reduces to a maximum over marked climbing chains with a fixed number of marks, then combines the one-mark base estimate, the truncation monotonicity of the Rajchgot code, the algorithm invariant that a heavy truncation stays heavy and the heavy-chain weight theorem, iterating the argument along the last link of each first component until the chain reaches w_0. Every ingredient is a source-local statement about the transfer-adjust-pass algorithm and the recursive Rajchgot code, so the argument is a genuine research mechanism rather than a routine corollary, and it is well above ordinary PhD qualifying combinatorics.",
  "status": "verified_editable_tex",
